      "number": 3,
      "title": "Compound Interest",
      "text": [
        "Discrete",
        "Continuous",
        "A = P(1 + r/n)^(nt)",
        "A = Pe^(rt)",
        "P = principal, r = rate (decimal), n = compounds/yr, t = years",
        "Same P, r, t. e ≈ 2.71828. Use when \"compounded continuously.\"",
        "Example: $2,500 at 3% for 20 years",
        "Monthly (n=12): A = 2500(1 + 0.03/12)^(240) = 2500(1.0025)^240 ≈ $4,551.89",
        "Continuous: A = 2500·e^(0.6) = 2500 × 1.82212 ≈ $4,555.30",
        "Calculator tip: Use parentheses! Enter (1.0025)^240, not 1.0025^240."
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "title": "Exponential ↔ Logarithmic Form",
      "text": [
        "b^y = x ⟺ log_b(x) = y The base stays the base!",
        "Exp → Log",
        "Log → Exp",
        "25^(5/2) = 3125 → log₂₅(3125) = 5/2",
        "log₄(2048) = 5.5 → 4^5.5 = 2048",
        "Solve: ln x = 4",
        "Solve: 2^x = 13",
        "x = e⁴ ≈ 54.598",
        "x = ln(13)/ln(2) ≈ 3.700"
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "title": "Angle Conversions",
      "text": [
        "DMS ↔ Decimal",
        "Radians ↔ Degrees",
        "DMS → Dec: D + M/60 + S/3600",
        "37°41'11\" = 37 + 41/60 + 11/3600 = 37.6864°",
        "Dec → DMS: take decimal × 60 each step",
        "36.3492° → 36° + 0.3492×60 = 20.952'",
        "→ 20' + 0.952×60 = 57\" → 36°20'57\"",
        "Deg → Rad: × π/180",
        "163.9° × π/180 ≈ 2.86 rad",
        "Rad → Deg: × 180/π",
        "2.7 rad × 180/π ≈ 154.7°",
        "Common: 30°=π/6 45°=π/4 60°=π/3 90°=π/2 180°=π 360°=2π"
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "title": "Arc Length & Sector Area",
      "text": [
        "Arc Length",
        "s = rθ",
        "r=5.7, θ=65° → θ=1.1345 rad → s=5.7×1.1345 ≈ 6.5",
        "Sector Area",
        "A = ½r²θ",
        "r=10, θ=3π/5 → A=½×100×(3π/5) ≈ 94.2",
        "⚠ θ MUST be in radians! Convert degrees first: θ_rad = θ_deg × π/180"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit2e/slide-06-1.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "title": "Triangle Area: Heron's Formula",
      "text": [
        "s = (a+b+c)/2 A = √[s(s−a)(s−b)(s−c)]",
        "Example: a = 1.5 cm, b = 1.3 cm, c = 2.1 cm",
        "s = (1.5 + 1.3 + 2.1)/2 = 4.9/2 = 2.45",
        "s−a = 0.95, s−b = 1.15, s−c = 0.35",
        "A = √(2.45 × 0.95 × 1.15 × 0.35) = √(0.937) ≈ 1.0 cm²",
        "Use Heron's when you know all 3 sides but NOT the height."
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "title": "Trapezoid Area (Multi-Step)",
      "text": [
        "A = ½(b₁ + b₂)h (may need Pythagorean Thm for h)",
        "Ex: b₁=4.5, b₂=10.1, slant=7.0 m",
        "Step 1: d = b₂ − b₁ = 5.6 m",
        "Step 2: h² + 5.6² = 7.0²",
        "h² = 49 − 31.36 = 17.64 → h = 4.2 m",
        "Step 3: A = ½(4.5+10.1)(4.2)",
        "A = ½(14.6)(4.2) = 30.66 m²"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit2e/slide-08-1.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "title": "Parallel Lines & Proportional Segments",
      "text": [
        "If parallel lines cut transversals, corresponding segments are proportional: AB/BD = AC/CE",
        "Example: AB = 40, BD = 45, AC = 37. Find CE and DC.",
        "Set up proportion:",
        "40/45 = 37/CE",
        "CE = 37 × 45/40 = 41.6 m",
        "DC = CE − AC = 41.6 − 37 = 4.6 m"
      ],
      "images": [],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "title": "Circle Theorems: Arcs & Angles",
      "text": [
        "Central angle = intercepted arc",
        "Inscribed angle = ½(intercepted arc)",
        "Intersecting chords: ∠ = ½(arc₁ + arc₂)",
        "Semicircle: diameter → arc = 180°"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit2e/slide-10-1.png"
      ],
      "speaker_notes": []
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "title": "Linear & Angular Speed",
      "text": [
        "Angular speed",
        "ω = θ/t (rad/time)",
        "1 rev = 2π radians",
        "Linear speed",
        "v = rω",
        "distance per unit time at edge",
        "Example: 350 RPM, r = 3 ft",
        "ω = 350 × 2π = 700π rad/min",
        "v = 3 × 700π = 2100π ≈ 6,597 ft/min",
        "→ 6,597 × 60 ÷ 5280 ≈ 75.0 mph"
      ],
      "images": [
        "assets/math130unit2e/slide-11-1.png"
